    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d434-a2">

                <pb facs="0664" n="564" sameAs="frus:frus1884/pg564"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2 in No. 381.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Eyres to Lieutenant-Colonel W.
                    Everett.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Van</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1884-03-31"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">March</hi> 31,
                    1884</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have received news from Bitlis to the
                    effect that Meza Bey, father of Moussa Bey, has been dismissed from his post of
                    Caimma kam, of Modkan. The defterdar of Bitlis, Husseim Bey, has also been
                    dismissed.</p>
                <p>The governor-general, Arif Pasha, lately sent a summons to Moussa Bey to appear
                    before the criminal court and stand his trial for the attack on the American
                    missionaries. No attention was paid to this summons, and zaptiehs were sent to
                    arrest him, but Moussa Bey refused to accompany them, and the zaptiehs returned
                    without effecting their purpose.</p>
                <p>I have &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>H. C. A. EYRES.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
